.TH synapse 1 "01 Jun 2022" "SYNAPSE SYNAPSE_VERSION" "SYNAPSE Manual"

.SH NAME
.B synapse
- High-performance reverse proxy and firewall

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B synapse
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Synapse is a high-performance reverse proxy and firewall built with Rust, featuring XDP-based packet filtering, dynamic access rules, threat intelligence integration, and advanced routing capabilities. It can operate in reverse proxy mode or firewall-only mode, providing ultra-low latency protection at the kernel level.

Some of the features provided by Synapse are:

.RS
.nf
- XDP-based packet filtering for kernel-level protection
- HTTP/HTTPS reverse proxy with TLS support
- Dynamic access rules with automatic updates
- Threat intelligence integration
- CAPTCHA protection (hCaptcha, reCAPTCHA, Cloudflare Turnstile)
- Content scanning with ClamAV integration
- Automatic TLS certificate management (ACME/Let's Encrypt)
- Advanced upstream routing with service discovery
- Hot-reloadable configuration
.RE

.SH FILES
.TP
.I
/etc/synapse/config.yaml
.TP
.I
/etc/synapse/upstreams.yaml
.TP
.I
/usr/bin/synapse
.TP
.I
/var/lib/synapse/
.TP
.I
/var/log/synapse/

.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.PP
The activity performed using this utility is logged in the systemd journal and can be viewed with:
.B journalctl -u synapse
.PP
Configuration files are located in /etc/synapse/

